      <h3 class="section-title">CITY OF BOSTON SITES</h3>
      <p>Reading up on these sites will transform you from a new Bostonian into a true Bostonian.</p>
      <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
        <li class="list-item"><strong>Office of Immigrant Advancement</strong><br><span data-field="oia_url">{{ oia_url }}</span></li>
        <li class="list-item"><strong>Boston Housing Authority</strong><br><span data-field="bha_url">{{ bha_url }}</span></li>
        <li class="list-item"><strong>SPARK</strong><br><span data-field="spark_url">{{ spark_url }}</span></li>
        <li class="list-item"><strong>Suffolk Cares Food Pantry</strong><br>73 Tremont Street, 12th Floor</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="column">
      <h3 class="section-title">WORKING WITH YOUR ROOMMATE(S)</h3>
      <p>When you live with someone, it is important to have a good relationship with them. If you are sharing a place with someone, you should consider creating a roommate agreement. This is a contract that outlines the expectations for and responsibilities to the other person. It is essential to maintain open and honest communication with your roommate(s). You might want to hold weekly house meetings to air potential problems and to find solutions.</p>

      <h3 class="section-title">SEEKING HELP</h3>
      <p>If you are experiencing trouble with your living situation and you feel that you need outside help, OCHO may refer you to another resource to resolve the conflict.</p>

      <h3 class="section-title">GRADUATE STUDENT ORGANIZATIONS</h3>
      <p>Suffolk also runs graduate student societies that promote professional development, networking, and social activities. Graduate students—all of whom live off-campus—may participate in these groups.</p>
      <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
        <li class="list-item">Association of Professional Latinos for America (ALPFA)</li>
        <li class="list-item">Chinese Students & Scholars Association</li>
        <li class="list-item">Crime and Justice Graduate Student Association</li>
        <li class="list-item">Future Healthcare Leaders Association</li>
        <li class="list-item">Master of Public Administration Student Association</li>
        <li class="list-item">MBA Association</li>
        <li class="list-item">National Association of Women</li>
        <li class="list-item">Suffolk Asian Business Club</li>
        <li class="list-item">Suffolk University Graduate Business Association</li>
      </ul>
      <p>In addition to the Student Bar Association, Suffolk offers a wide range of organizations listed at <span data-field="org_list_url">{{ org_list_url }}</span>.</p>
